    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23290" root="شور" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شِيَارٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شُورَةٌ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also a name given by the
Arabs to <i>Saturday,</i> (S in this art., and K in art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شير</span>,) in the Time of Ignorance: (TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شير</span>:)
pl. [of pauc.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشْيُرٌ</span> and [of mult.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شُيُرٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شِيرٌ</span>:
(Zj, K:) accord. to Zj, you may say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَلَاثَةُ شِيرٍ</span>
[<i>Three Saturdays,</i> using <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شِير</span> as a pl. of pauc.]:
so in the Tekmileh. (TA.)

